  "version": 1,
  "questionId": "q23",
  "speechText": "At a high level, LangChain gives higher-level building blocks for models, prompts, tools, and middleware. LangGraph is more about lower-level, stateful orchestration for long-running workflows, with durable execution and human-in-the-loop support. StrangeLoop is broader. It includes Studio for configuration and control, an Engine for execution, and a clear boundary between the app and its domain tools. So my simple summary is: LangGraph is more an orchestration framework. StrangeLoop is closer to a production agent platform.",
